  "question": {
    "text": "In a closed circuit there is only a coil of inductance $L$ and resistance $100 \\Omega$. The coil is situated in a uniform magnetic field. All on a sudden, the magnetic flux linked with the circuit changes by $5 \\mathrm{Weber}$. What amount of charge will flow in the circuit as a result?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pXsfb",
      "text": "$500 \\mathrm{C}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3udt7",
      "text": "$0.05 \\mathrm{C}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ByqVO",
      "text": "$20 \\mathrm{C}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FgxG7",
      "text": "Value of $L$ is to be known to find the charge flown",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Emf $=-\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\phi}{\\mathrm{dt}}($ Faraday's Law $)$\n$\\mathrm{i}_{\\text {induced }}=\\frac{\\mathrm{Emf}}{\\mathrm{R}}=-\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\phi}{\\mathrm{dt}} \\times \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{dq}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}} \\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\phi}{\\mathrm{dt}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{dq}=-\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\phi}{\\mathrm{R}} \\Rightarrow \\int \\mathrm{dq}=-\\int \\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\phi}{\\mathrm{R}}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{q}_{\\text {flown }}=\\frac{\\phi_{\\mathrm{i}}-\\phi_{\\mathrm{f}}}{\\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{5 \\text { weber }}{100}=0.05 \\mathrm{C} .$",
    "image": null
  },
